    {
      "id": "Tu2zJilfgmo_ku5ydOCak",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1787.693466806095,
      "y": 20396.73108044801,
      "width": 1074.5119932182365,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cLLp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 813700303,
      "version": 779,
      "versionNonce": 2137774494,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033857335,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Consider HELLO Segment get Dropped and WORLD Segment get reached to\nreciver so instead of Next expected seq no as 14 reciver continue sending\nnext req seq number as 4 so sender knows that that segment late pahuchega\nya wo drop ho gaya hai. technically to wo pahucha hi nhi hai kyunki reciver ko\nabhi tk mila hi nhi hai. and then sender retransmit it and receiver get that\nthen receiver ask for next seq number as 14 bcz 9 it already get",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Consider HELLO Segment get Dropped and WORLD Segment get reached to reciver so instead of Next expected seq no as 14 reciver continue sending next req seq number as 4 so sender knows that that segment late pahuchega ya wo drop ho gaya hai. technically to wo pahucha hi nhi hai kyunki reciver ko abhi tk mila hi nhi hai. and then sender retransmit it and receiver get that then receiver ask for next seq number as 14 bcz 9 it already get",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wjSSQVYMoT_VMuznjPSbV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1787.693466977975,
      "y": 20694.449099211353,
      "width": 1138.3189556704845,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cLLq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1393956481,
      "version": 427,
      "versionNonce": 1628346178,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033857335,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTE In Lect: Repeatedly receiving the same ACK number is called a \"Duplicate\nACK\". It's one of the primary ways TCP detects packet loss and triggers\ncongestion control (We'll understand exactly how this work in the \"Congestion\nControl\" video :))",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTE In Lect: Repeatedly receiving the same ACK number is called a \"Duplicate ACK\". It's one of the primary ways TCP detects packet loss and triggers congestion control (We'll understand exactly how this work in the \"Congestion Control\" video :))",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "iNRJXs1u6Dq6fybTuBgTH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -632.8234405498081,
      "y": 20421.45976023336,
      "width": 1083.38037109375,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cLLr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 768188129,
      "version": 196,
      "versionNonce": 1849357790,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033857335,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is how ack number helps to detect that packet get lost or retransmission",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is how ack number helps to detect that packet get lost or retransmission",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cll9X15edHrG0MNOFXJp3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1786.8120607220203,
      "y": 21041.834042485294,
      "width": 797.929129377342,
      "height": 260.7737557060902,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cLLs",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1371096111,
      "version": 230,
      "versionNonce": 1602117378,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033857335,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Together, Seq and ACK Numbers\n- Detect lost segments\n- Detect duplicate segments\n- Enable retransmission of missing data\n- Gaurantee ordered delivery of data",
      "fontSize": 41.72380091297445,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Together, Seq and ACK Numbers\n- Detect lost segments\n- Detect duplicate segments\n- Enable retransmission of missing data\n- Gaurantee ordered delivery of data",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
