    {
      "id": "DQbZ4p-f4PKOpDL9JTN5S",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1248.2078211443254,
      "y": 4011.6167503289407,
      "width": 1035.1767928341228,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cLPq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 856765266,
      "version": 975,
      "versionNonce": 2049509982,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033872407,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Uske liye hum use karte hi DF -> don't fragment (IP Packet header) -> 1(set)\n\nhumne 1500 ka packet bheja MTU: 1460 ko milathen wo usko drop kar dega kyunki wo usko fragment kar\nnhi skta and original IP Size > MTU so it drop it and it notify the client that i cannot fagment it but i\nneed to fragment it to send ahead notify like \"Fragmentation is needed my MTU is 1420\" this reply go\nwith help of ICMP protocol\n\nthen firse source se 1420 MTU ka packet banega with DF set to 1 so is baar wo is MTU:1420 router ko\nto pass kar lega lekin aage if chota MTU wala router hoga then drop karega and notify karega then loop\nchalta rhega until it reaches destination\n\nthis is how my client knows the minimum MTU of this path\n\nthis is how it prevents the fragmentation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Uske liye hum use karte hi DF -> don't fragment (IP Packet header) -> 1(set)\n\nhumne 1500 ka packet bheja MTU: 1460 ko milathen wo usko drop kar dega kyunki wo usko fragment kar nhi skta and original IP Size > MTU so it drop it and it notify the client that i cannot fagment it but i need to fragment it to send ahead notify like \"Fragmentation is needed my MTU is 1420\" this reply go with help of ICMP protocol\n\nthen firse source se 1420 MTU ka packet banega with DF set to 1 so is baar wo is MTU:1420 router ko to pass kar lega lekin aage if chota MTU wala router hoga then drop karega and notify karega then loop chalta rhega until it reaches destination\n\nthis is how my client knows the minimum MTU of this path\n\nthis is how it prevents the fragmentation",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
