      "seed": 1030969876,
      "version": 468,
      "versionNonce": 2019712130,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033872409,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Similar to the Receive Window(RWND), the Congestion window (cwnd) is also measured in\nbytes. So, In this examoke, cend = 1 means 1 byte. In real-world TCP, this is typically 1\nMSS (e.g., aaround 1460 bytes). However, for simplicity we've assumed 1MSS= 1bytes\nthroughout this example to keep the math easy",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Similar to the Receive Window(RWND), the Congestion window (cwnd) is also measured in bytes. So, In this examoke, cend = 1 means 1 byte. In real-world TCP, this is typically 1 MSS (e.g., aaround 1460 bytes). However, for simplicity we've assumed 1MSS= 1bytes throughout this example to keep the math easy",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
