      "seed": 104583700,
      "version": 312,
      "versionNonce": 1964973086,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786033872410,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How TCP can detect Congestion before it happenes?\n\nECN (Explicit Congestion Notification)\n- Traditional TCP detects congestion after packet loss occues\n- ECN allows routers to indicate congestion before dropping packets\n- Helps reduce unnecesary packet loss and retransmission",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How TCP can detect Congestion before it happenes?\n\nECN (Explicit Congestion Notification)\n- Traditional TCP detects congestion after packet loss occues\n- ECN allows routers to indicate congestion before dropping packets\n- Helps reduce unnecesary packet loss and retransmission",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
